nakoniukhova staff 137097216 Nov  9 22:37 thread_history_1.sqlite\n-rw-r--r--   1 valentinakoniukhova staff     32768 Nov  9 22:38 thread_history_1.sqlite-shm\n-rw-r--r--   1 valentinakoniukhova staff   1849912 Nov  9 22:39 thread_history_1.sqlite-wal\ndrwxr-xr-x   5 valentinakoniukhova staff       160 Nov  9 10:17 tmp\n/opt/homebrew/lib/node_modules/@openai/codex/bin/codex.js","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"037fa454-08e5-4307-917f-fb36989bfe59","uuid":"a312a7c9-65ef-4d18-b6d7-4e85b9bae98b","timestamp":"2026-11-10T01:39:20.667Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# agent-evals\n\nA small harness that runs coding agents on short tasks and keeps everything a\nrun produced, so the runs can be graded and compared later. It lives in\n`~/evals/agent-evals` on the eval Mac.\n\n`./run.sh <task> <lane> [rep]` copies `tasks/<task>/` into a scratch folder in\n`/tmp`, runs the lane's agent there with `tasks/<task>.prompt`, and writes the\nrun folder `runs/<task>-<lane>-r<rep>/`:\n\n- `prompt.txt`, `agent.log` (the agent's JSON event stream), `agent.err`,\n  `meta.json` (exit code, seconds);\n- `final.txt`, the agent's last message, for the Codex lanes;\n- `answer.json`, written by `check_answer.py`: the final answer the graders\n  read (from `final.txt` for Codex, from the event stream for Kimi).\n\nLanes:\n\n- `codex`: Codex CLI (`codex exec --json`), unsandboxed.\n- `kimi`: Kimi Code. Its output goes to Moonshot, so its shell runs under the\n  macOS sandbox profile `sandbox/agent.sb` (no reading or writing the real\n  home), with an empty scratch HOME. Kimi's own install and sessions live in\n  `~/.kimi-code`, which the profile opens.\n\nCodex logs in with an API key from the environment (`CODEX_API_KEY`), so it\nneeds nothing from the home folder.\n\"\"\"The final answer of a run, as the graders read it: final.txt (Codex lanes), else the last assistant message in\nthe Kimi stream-json log. usage: check_answer.py <run folder>  ->  {\"final\": \"...\", \"source\": \"...\"}\"\"\"\nimport json, os, sys\n\nR = sys.argv[1]\ndef read(p):\n    try: return open(p, errors=\"replace\").read()\n    except OSError: return \"\"\n\nfinal, source = read(os.path.join(R, \"final.txt\")), \"final.txt\"\nlane = json.loads(read(os.path.join(R, \"meta.json\")) or \"{}\").get(\"lane\", \"\")\nif not final.strip() and lane.startswith(\"kimi\"):\n    source = \"agent.log\"\n    for line in reversed(read(os.path.join(R, \"agent.log\")).splitlines()):\n        try: d = json.loads(line)\n        except ValueError: continue\n        if d.get(\"role\") == \"assistant\" and isinstance(d.get(\"content\"), str) and d[\"content\"].strip():\n            final = d[\"content\"]; break\nprint(json.dumps({\"final\": final, \"source\": source if final.strip() else \"none\"}))\nruns:\n\ntasks:\nfizz\nfizz.prompt\nruns/*\n!runs/.keep\nwhich: no kimi in (/opt/homebrew/opt/coreutils/libexec/gnubin:/opt/homebrew/opt/findutils/libexec/gnubin:/opt/homebrew/opt/gawk/libexec/gnubin:/opt/homebrew/opt/gnu-sed/libexec/gnubin:/opt/homebrew/opt/gnu-tar/libexec/gnubin:/opt/homebrew/opt/gnu-which/libexec/gnubin:/opt/homebrew/opt/grep/libexec/gnubin:/opt/homebrew/opt/coreutils/libexec/gnubin:/opt/homebrew/opt/findutils/libexec/gnubin:/opt/homebrew/opt/gawk/libexec/gnubin:/opt/homebrew/opt/gnu-sed/libexec/gnubin:/opt/homebrew/opt/gnu-tar/libexec/gnubin:/opt/homebrew/opt/gnu-which/libexec/gnubin:/opt/homebrew/opt/grep/libexec/gnubin:/opt/homebrew/opt/coreutils/libexec/gnubin:/opt/homebrew/opt/findutils/libexec/gnubin:/opt/homebrew/opt/gawk/libexec/gnubin:/opt/homebrew/opt/gnu-sed/libexec/gnubin:/opt/homebrew/opt/gnu-tar/libexec/gnubin:/opt/homebrew/opt/gnu-which/libexec/gnubin:/opt/homebrew/opt/grep/libexec/gnubin:/opt/homebrew/opt/coreutils/libexec/gnubin:/opt/homebrew/opt/findutils/libexec/gnubin:/opt/homebrew/opt/gawk/libexec/gnubin:/opt/homebrew/opt/gnu-sed/libexec/gnubin:/opt/homebrew/opt/gnu-tar/libexec/gnubin:/opt/homebrew/opt/gnu-which/libexec/gnubin:/opt/homebre