{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QubcGkrGmnqjbShsY6FBp9","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /private/tmp/h-jyR1Vp/README.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"037fa454-08e5-4307-917f-fb36989bfe59","uuid":"629c121d-d12a-4522-895a-b67384f10676","timestamp":"2026-11-10T01:41:45.663Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-jyR1Vp/README.md","oldString":"- `codex`: Codex CLI (`codex exec --json`), unsandboxed.\n- `kimi`:","newString":"- `codex`: Codex CLI (`codex exec --json`), unsandboxed.\n- `codex-sandbox`: the same Codex command, run under the same profile\n  `sandbox/agent.sb` with an empty scratch HOME. Codex's state lives in a\n  scratch `CODEX_HOME`, into which only `~/.codex/auth.json` (the login token)\n  is copied; the copy is deleted after the run. The token is therefore readable\n  by the agent's shell, and the network is open. Config, MCP servers and\n  history in the real `~/.codex` are not visible to the run.\n- `kimi`:","originalFile":"# agent-evals\n\nA small harness that runs coding agents on short tasks and keeps everything a\nrun produced, so the runs can be graded and compared later. It lives in\n`~/evals/agent-evals` on the eval Mac.\n\n`./run.sh <task> <lane> [rep]` copies `tasks/<task>/` into a scratch folder in\n`/tmp`, runs the lane's agent there with `tasks/<task>.prompt`, and writes the\nrun folder `runs/<task>-<lane>-r<rep>/`:\n\n- `prompt.txt`, `agent.log` (the agent's JSON event stream), `agent.err`,\n  `meta.json` (exit code, seconds);\n- `final.txt`, the agent's last message, for the Codex lanes;\n- `answer.json`, written by `check_answer.py`: the final answer the graders\n  read (from `final.txt` for Codex, from the event stream for Kimi).\n\nLanes:\n\n- `codex`: Codex CLI (`codex exec --json`), unsandboxed.\n- `kimi`: Kimi Code. Its output goes to Moonshot, so its shell runs under the\n  macOS sandbox profile `sandbox/agent.sb` (no reading or writing the real\n  home), with an empty scratch HOME. Kimi's own install and sessions live in\n  `~/.kimi-code`, which the profile opens.\n\nCodex logs in with an API key from the environment (`CODEX_API_KEY`), so it\nneeds nothing from the home folder.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":17,"oldLines":6,"newStart":17,"newLines":12,"lines":[" Lanes:"," "," - `codex`: Codex CLI (`codex exec --json`), unsandboxed.","+- `codex-sandbox`: the same Codex command, run under the same profile","+  `sandbox/agent.sb` with an empty scratch HOME. Codex's state lives in a","+  scratch `CODEX_HOME`, into which only `~/.codex/auth.json` (the login token)","+  is copied; the copy is deleted after the run. The token is therefore readable","+  by the agent's shell, and the network is open. Config, MCP servers and","+  history in the real `~/.codex` are not visible to the run."," - `kimi`: Kimi Code. Its output goes to Moonshot, so its shell runs under the","   macOS sandbox profile `sandbox/agent.sb` (no reading or writing the real","   home), with an empty scratch HOME. Kimi's own install and sessions live in"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01QubcGkrGmnqjbShsY6FBp9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
