re readable\n  by the agent's shell, and the network is open. Config, MCP servers and\n  history in the real `~/.codex` are not visible to the run.\n- `kimi`: Kimi Code. Its output goes to Moonshot, so its shell runs under the\n  macOS sandbox profile `sandbox/agent.sb` (no reading or writing the real\n  home), with an empty scratch HOME. Kimi's own install and sessions live in\n  `~/.kimi-code`, which the profile opens.\n\nCodex logs in with an API key from the environment (`CODEX_API_KEY`), so it\nneeds nothing from the home folder.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":28,"oldLines":5,"newStart":28,"newLines":6,"lines":["   home), with an empty scratch HOME. Kimi's own install and sessions live in","   `~/.kimi-code`, which the profile opens."," ","-Codex logs in with an API key from the environment (`CODEX_API_KEY`), so it","-needs nothing from the home folder.","+The `codex` lane needs nothing from the home folder when `CODEX_API_KEY` is set","+in the environment. On the eval Mac it is not set; codex uses the ChatGPT login","+in `~/.codex/auth.json` instead, which is why `codex-sandbox` copies that file."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Kc5uQSzCNbRmgU5SshyBSx","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
